      "message": "fix(sim): pack the playback picture's base from the uncut stock\n\nThe calculation before playback (#2181) ran before the worker packed the\nsession's constant GPU lattice, so the base was packed from the stock cut\nto the end of the program. The pack's eikonal pass writes max(mesh, cut)\ninto the mesh layer and later frames only lift cells over it: every\nframe drew the finished part, which sits inside the model, and the stock\nbody was never seen. The base is packed from the uncut stock again,\nbefore the calculation.\n\nPinned by stock_play_precalc::the_picture_at_the_start_is_the_uncut_stock_after_the_calculation,\nwhich reads the packed lattice the eye draws at move 0.\n\nFixes #2396\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
